-- title:
--   Actual stopped BV C1 compensated negative Lévy jump has L1 and zero mean under original strategy and Lévy energy
-- statement:
--   On the original probability space and right-continuous filtration, the genuine intrinsic marked negative jump measure minus the genuine samplewise predictable Lévy compensator is an integrable, mean-zero term for the stopped discounted BV C1 controlled process. The original dividend strategy, C1 continuation at nonnegative reserves, and actual quadratic Lévy energy imply the signed kernel's product measurability and the finite negative mark tail, while local compact-strip Lipschitz and finite true predictable clock imply the full intensity L1. The only missing original probabilistic input is the precise strict-future marked rectangle law, stated honestly as hFuture, plus true stopping and interior localisation. Does not replace the original sample space or assume a martingale conclusion.
